WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:13.940
A multi-camera AI monitoring architecture is the complete system that receives several video feeds, analyzes selected frames, stores footage and event metadata, sends alerts, and supports human review.

2
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:21.080
Processing may be local, distributed to edge devices, or split between local and approved cloud services.

3
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:34.880
The components include cameras, NVRs, RTSP streams, networks, edge devices, servers, CPUs or accelerators, models, storage, dashboards, logs, and alert channels.

4
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:41.860
Architecture determines how these pieces share identity, time, capacity, policy, and failure handling.

5
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:47.580
A single-camera experiment can succeed while an operational fleet fails.

6
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:56.800
One demonstration may ignore stream drops, time drift, storage growth, model updates, alert duplication, reviewer workload, and hardware saturation.

7
00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:00.020
A production design has to manage all of them continuously.

8
00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.340
Scaling also changes privacy and security.

9
00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:08.480
More cameras create more coverage, credentials, footage, and users.

10
00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:16.660
The design should limit collection to legitimate areas, protect every data path, and make access and retention visible to governance.

11
00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:22.300
AI models assist with detection, description, grouping, and prioritization.

12
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.640
They do not establish identity, intent, or wrongdoing by themselves.

13
00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:32.180
Important alerts need context and accountable human confirmation before action.

14
00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:38.940
Multi-camera monitoring is therefore an architecture and operations problem, not simply a model-selection problem.

15
00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:51.120
A strong system balances useful visibility with compute, storage, latency, resilience, alert quality, privacy, security, and responsible use.
